WEBVTT

00:01.800 --> 00:05.365
Fractured Order is an economic statecraft seminar game.

00:05.715 --> 00:13.349
Teams read a changing strategic environment, make decisions, negotiate, and adapt across several phases of play.

00:13.899 --> 00:18.437
Run through side channels and slide decks, that activity fractures fast:

00:18.587 --> 00:23.252
who decided what, who owns the next step, and what changed the course of play.

00:24.502 --> 00:27.854
Plenum is the operational layer that holds it together.

00:28.054 --> 00:31.439
One live session, in the browser, shared by every role.

00:32.589 --> 00:33.860
Four teams play.

00:34.060 --> 00:36.231
Blue and Red, the competing powers.

00:36.381 --> 00:39.590
Green, their partners, in Asia-Pacific and Europe.

00:39.740 --> 00:44.551
And Industry: agriculture, telecommunications and biotechnology.

00:45.601 --> 00:48.724
Inside each team, every seat has a clear job.

00:48.924 --> 00:51.311
The Scribe records the team's decisions.

00:51.411 --> 00:54.682
The Facilitator reviews them, and submits to White Cell.

00:54.782 --> 00:59.324
The Notetaker captures observations, team dynamics and alliances.

01:00.374 --> 01:02.623
Above the teams sit the control cells.

01:02.823 --> 01:09.829
White Cell runs the clock, gates each phase, answers requests for information, and reviews every submission.

01:10.079 --> 01:15.116
The Game Master creates sessions, monitors participants and exports the data.

01:16.266 --> 01:18.978
Play opens with Strategic Orientation.

01:19.128 --> 01:25.792
Blue, for example, chooses its own course, Pressure, Stabilization or Reframe, and forecasts Red's.

01:26.042 --> 01:29.764
White Cell holds Move 1 until the orientations are in.

01:30.214 --> 01:38.503
Then, through Moves 1 to 3, teams draft actions and proposals, negotiate in threads, and send requests for information.

01:38.753 --> 01:47.095
Every record moves through visible stages: draft, forwarded to the Facilitator, submitted to White Cell, deliberation, completed.

01:48.245 --> 01:52.648
Submitted actions go to PLI for multi-track adjudication.

01:52.848 --> 01:57.522
Subject-matter experts review each track, and approve or edit the result.

01:57.772 --> 02:02.416
Consequences come back as news in the Tribe Street Journal, and teams adapt.

02:03.666 --> 02:06.394
When play ends, the session becomes evidence.

02:06.594 --> 02:13.303
Orientations, actions, proposals, threads and requests export as one validated dataset:

02:13.353 --> 02:20.147
a browser report, a formal PDF workflow, and CSV, JSON and JSONL for research.

02:20.397 --> 02:24.653
Where history was reconstructed rather than captured, the report says so.

02:26.003 --> 02:29.060
Plenum doesn't replace judgment or facilitation.

02:29.210 --> 02:33.172
It gives them structure: coordinated, observable, reviewable.

02:33.922 --> 02:35.867
Fractured Order. On Plenum.
